  "description": "Wide, deep water and three jetties to launch from. The open water grows from 150 to 190 and then 230 units, and each far bank sits a little lower than the jetty. Build speed on the bank, stay on the throttle to the end of the planks, and keep the bike level in the air so you land on both wheels on the far bank. Coming up short means a swim.",
  "lesson": "Jumping over wide deep water.",
  "alsoNew": "Moderate rain, jetty and rowing boat props.",
